Description: faithful lightweight digital code rain for XScreenSaver
 MatrixCode is a standalone OpenGL/GLX XScreenSaver hack inspired by the flat,
 sparse digital rain aesthetic of the original Matrix films.
 .
 It uses an original clean-room atlas of narrow katakana-inspired forms,
 mirrored variants, digits, and punctuation. Stationary glyphs are illuminated
 by independently falling pulses with pale heads, irregular green tails, and a
 lightweight two-pass glow. No film assets or third-party fonts are included.
 .
 The fixed-function renderer avoids mandatory shaders and framebuffers, making
 it suitable for old or low-power X11 systems.
